      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Altogether 117 case reports were analyzed and 32 patients with associated gastric or duodenal ulcer and coronary heart disease (CHD) as well as 48 controls suffering from gastric or duodenal ulcer were examined. A relationship was established between the clinical picture and the course of associated ulcer disease and CHD and the time of ulcer disease onset. Patients suffering from ulcer disease that occurred at a young age manifested the typical clinical picture, seasonal exacerbations while ulcer exacerbations were often accompanied by CHD exacerbations. Ulcer disease that developed in CHD patients often runs an atypical or asymptomatic and a longer course marked by more frequently occurring ulcer complications. Ulcer occurs in the stomach more frequently, with gastric secretion being considerably lowered. Analysis of the above-enumerated characteristic features makes it possible to individualize the treatment of patients with combined ulcer disease and CHD."},
